<section class="hero compact">
    <p class="eyebrow">EMERALD / SYSTEM AUDIT</p>
    <h1>revdep</h1>

    <p class="lead">
        Scan installed binaries and libraries for broken reverse dependencies.
    </p>

    <div class="command-line"># revdep [options]</div>
</section>

<section class="doc">
    <h2 id="help">
        <code>revdep help</code>
    </h2>

    <pre><code>Usage:
    revdep <options> [<arg>]

Options:
    -a, --all                       print all affected files
    -r, --rebuild                   rebuild &amp; reinstall broken package
    -f, --no-filter                 skip filter (exclude) dirs, files and libraries
    -e, --exclude <pkg1 pkg2 pkgN>  exclude package when rebuild (use with -r/--rebuild)
    -y, --yes                       dont ask user confirmation to rebuild package (use with -r/--rebuild)
    -h, --help                      print this help message</code></pre>

    <h2 id="usage">Usage</h2>

    <pre><code>revdep --help
revdep</code></pre>

    <p>
        Configure exclusions in <code>/etc/revdep.conf</code> and optional files
        under <code>/etc/revdep.d/*.conf</code> and <code>/usr/lib/revdep.d/*.conf</code>
        (the latter installed by ports). The scan can inspect shared
        libraries and language modules; review exclusions carefully so a real
        broken dependency is not hidden.
    </p>
</section>
